# ── Why this file exists ──────────────────────────────────────────
# Stage 1 of the Dockerfile runs `npm ci` and only then `COPY . .`. Without these
# exclusions the host's own node_modules — installed for the developer's platform,
# not the image's linux/* — is copied straight over the tree npm just installed,
# so the shipped bundle is built from whatever happened to be on the build machine
# rather than from package-lock.json.
#
# Keep in step with the Dockerfile: anything a build stage copies must NOT appear
# below. Stage 1 (SPA) needs package.json, package-lock.json, index.html,
# vite.config.ts, tsconfig.json and src/. Stage 2 (BFF) needs bff/. Nothing else is
# read at build time — docker-compose.yaml bind-mounts configs/ and resources/ at
# run time, which this file does not affect.

# ── Host dependency trees — reinstalled inside the image ──────────
node_modules
bff/**/node_modules

# ── Build output — regenerated by `npm run build` ─────────────────
# A stale copy must never be shipped in place of the build's own output.
dist
target

# ── Local credentials and TLS material ────────────────────────────
# setup.sh output: developer-generated, untracked, and bind-mounted at run time.
# Must never be baked into an image layer, where a rotated or removed secret can
# silently resurface on a `docker compose up` without `--build`.
resources

# ── Config / environment (mounted at runtime via volume) ──────────
# .env matters beyond tidiness: Vite loads it at build time and inlines any
# APIP_AIW_* key it defines (vite.config.ts envPrefix), so a developer's local
# file would otherwise be baked into a production bundle. No .env is committed;
# every deployment configures the BFF through the config.toml it mounts at
# /etc/ai-workspace/config.toml.
.env
.env.*
api-platform.env
docker-compose.yaml

# ── Tests and reports (~20MB of context, read by nothing in the build) ──
cypress
cypress.config.js
cypress.env.json
reports
coverage
**/*.test.ts
**/*.test.tsx

# ── Build tooling and release packaging ───────────────────────────
Makefile
VERSION
distribution
production

# ── Documentation ─────────────────────────────────────────────────
*.md

# ── Git / editor metadata ─────────────────────────────────────────
.git
.gitignore
.claude
.vscode
.idea
.DS_Store

# ── Logs ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
*.log
npm-debug.log*
